# WDLL practice (all agents)

For sprint-scale or program-scale work (multi-repo waves, multi-dispatch workstreams, anything whose "done" could be argued about afterward):

1. Before implementation, a WDLL doc must exist and be operator-approved: observable end state plus numbered acceptance items, each checkable by a specific observation. Template and full practice: `90_runbooks/wdll_practice.md`.
2. Every dispatch and PR cites the acceptance item numbers it is responsible for.
3. Adversarial review verifies deliverables against the cited WDLL items, not re-derived intent.
4. Scope changes are recorded as WDLL amendments with a one-line reason, never silently absorbed.
5. At close, re-grade the same card item by item (met, partial, dropped, with one line of evidence) and file the grading with the session close. The Start-vs-Finish diff is the drift record.
6. If the work touched a spine-model concept (atoms, calibration, lineage, access policy, license, capture jobs, tiles), add one entry to `_catalog/thesis_parity_ledger.md`.

Do not start building sprint-scale work without an approved WDLL. Do not estimate timeframes in WDLL items; stack items in execution order with dependencies named.
